# Per-Dockerfile ignore for backstage/Dockerfile. BuildKit prefers a <dockerfile>.dockerignore
# over the context-root .dockerignore, so this scopes ONLY the Backstage image build — the .NET
# image legs (which also use the repo root as context) are unaffected, and there is no repo-root
# .dockerignore to change their behaviour.
#
# Correctness does not depend on this file — the Dockerfile COPYs explicit paths (backstage/,
# contracts/catalog, contracts/openapi/{specs,internal}, infra/backstage/app-config.yaml) rather
# than `COPY . .`. This just keeps the repo-root context lean and deterministic by dropping the
# heavy, never-COPY'd artefacts (a stray local node_modules/dist/.git would otherwise bloat the
# context sent to the daemon).
.git
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/bin
**/obj
backstage/.yarn/cache
backstage/.yarn/install-state.gz
